WEBVTT

00:12.053 --> 00:13.805
♪ See the daylight ♪

00:15.223 --> 00:17.392
♪ Covering the sky ♪

00:18.852 --> 00:22.230
♪ Hear the wind say ♪

00:22.313 --> 00:26.484
♪ No matter what you do, my friend ♪

00:26.568 --> 00:29.571
♪ You know the world
Still needs your light ♪

00:29.654 --> 00:32.449
♪ Let it just shine ♪

00:32.532 --> 00:38.246
♪ You'll be free
From all the things you used to be ♪

00:40.040 --> 00:42.042
[bell clanging]

00:43.626 --> 00:48.381
DOONA!

00:51.134 --> 00:54.220
[cheering and applause]

01:21.206 --> 01:23.208
[somber music playing]

01:29.839 --> 01:32.342
[crowd cheering]

01:32.425 --> 01:34.427
[somber music continues]

01:54.572 --> 01:55.406
[gasps]

01:57.742 --> 01:59.119
[exhales]

02:05.458 --> 02:10.255
EPISODE 1
AN UNEXPECTED TWIST

02:15.760 --> 02:19.639
KOOK'S SEAFOOD HOUSE

02:19.722 --> 02:21.641
[pop music playing]

02:30.024 --> 02:31.901
KOOK'S SEAFOOD HOUSE
CEO KOOK SU-JIN

02:33.278 --> 02:35.446
So I, um, made business cards.

02:35.530 --> 02:37.991
- [chuckles]
- Ooh.

02:38.074 --> 02:40.535
I'm super jealous.
Twenty-one and a CEO already.

02:40.618 --> 02:43.037
Now that you're the boss,
you can pick your hours, huh?

02:43.121 --> 02:45.415
Maybe you could help my mom.
Her back is pretty bad.

02:45.498 --> 02:48.626
If you're so worried about your mother,
then why you moving all the way to Seoul?

02:49.127 --> 02:51.629
The drive to school from here
has been a lot.

02:51.713 --> 02:53.756
Now that my sister isn't in the hospital,

02:54.632 --> 02:57.343
I can live closer to school
and utilize that time better.

02:59.387 --> 03:00.513
Hey, Kooksu.

03:01.764 --> 03:02.765
Thank you.

03:03.349 --> 03:04.767
Take care of my mom, you hear?

03:04.851 --> 03:06.311
Don't worry about it, okay?

03:10.523 --> 03:13.943
If, by any chance, while you're in Seoul,
you happen to see Doona,

03:14.027 --> 03:15.695
dude, you gotta call me, all right?

03:15.778 --> 03:18.072
[boy] Yeah, right.
Like that would ever happen.

03:18.156 --> 03:20.950
WHEN THE ANSWERS INCLUDE
VERBS AND NON-VERBS

03:21.034 --> 03:24.746
Verbs are in the middle.
Nouns are… in front.

03:24.829 --> 03:25.705
[suitcase clatters]

03:25.788 --> 03:27.540
Oh, sorry about that.

03:31.878 --> 03:32.962
[sighs]

03:33.046 --> 03:35.048
[upbeat music playing]

03:59.781 --> 04:00.782
[sighs]

04:05.286 --> 04:06.871
LOVE AND DO WHAT YOU WILL

04:22.220 --> 04:23.346
Hello there.

04:27.183 --> 04:28.101
[clears throat]

04:41.239 --> 04:43.241
[keypad beeping]

04:44.200 --> 04:45.785
[fast beeping]

04:47.912 --> 04:49.539
[keypad beeping]

04:49.622 --> 04:51.124
[fast beeping]

04:54.210 --> 04:55.295
[boy exhales]

04:58.131 --> 05:00.133
[keypad beeping]

05:04.220 --> 05:06.222
- Oh.
- [door beeps]

05:06.889 --> 05:07.724
It worked.

05:21.779 --> 05:25.575
Hey, uh, you look familiar.
Do we know each other at all?

05:26.576 --> 05:28.328
[curious music playing]

05:29.329 --> 05:30.913
Oh, uh, I guess not.

05:32.123 --> 05:34.959
I think I had you confused
with someone I once knew.

05:36.711 --> 05:37.754
I'm sorry about that.

05:38.755 --> 05:41.299
Ah, just so you know,
I'm the new tenant on the second floor.

05:41.382 --> 05:42.717
I hope we become great neighbors.

05:42.800 --> 05:45.386
This is actually the first time
that I have left home.

05:47.013 --> 05:47.930
[sighs]

06:04.947 --> 06:06.908
PLEASE KNOCK

06:07.575 --> 06:08.451
Oh.

06:12.622 --> 06:14.499
Hi, I'm Lee Won-jun.
I'm the new tenant upstairs.

06:14.582 --> 06:16.709
[boy] Here. Please review the house rules.

06:17.460 --> 06:18.628
HOUSE RULES

06:18.711 --> 06:20.671
Specifically, number seven,
the laundry guidelines.

06:22.298 --> 06:25.676
Since you're upstairs,
you do your laundry on the rooftop, okay?

06:25.760 --> 06:28.096
[upbeat music playing]

06:28.971 --> 06:31.516
- Is that clear?
- Yes, it is. It's very clear, sir.

06:35.561 --> 06:36.646
[door closes]

06:40.650 --> 06:41.526
[Won-jun] Oh.

06:42.944 --> 06:44.821
- Newbie?
- Uh, yes.

06:44.904 --> 06:47.407
- It's really nice to meet--
- I'm a senior and a psych major.

06:48.074 --> 06:50.201
Taek, Taek, I'm Yun-taek.

06:51.244 --> 06:52.412
Seo Yun-taek.

06:53.204 --> 06:56.624
Okay, cool. So I'm Lee Won-jun,
second year, civil engineering.

06:56.707 --> 06:59.794
You have nothing to worry about here,
so let's just say

06:59.877 --> 07:01.421
you can just be yourself, freely.

07:01.504 --> 07:02.880
Live free, Won-jun.

07:03.423 --> 07:04.257
Okay?

07:04.340 --> 07:05.174
Uh-huh.

07:05.883 --> 07:06.801
Ah.

07:07.427 --> 07:08.261
Welcome.

07:08.761 --> 07:09.595
[grunts]

07:14.267 --> 07:15.393
- [urinating]
- Huh?

07:15.476 --> 07:16.561
Oh jeez.

07:19.272 --> 07:20.106
[sighs]

07:30.366 --> 07:32.368
- [Won-jun grunts]
- [stairs creaking]

07:37.081 --> 07:38.207
[sighs]

07:40.835 --> 07:42.837
[whistling]

07:44.922 --> 07:46.924
[vacuum whirring]

07:55.975 --> 07:58.561
Whoa! Ah! No, wait!
Don't fall. Don't fall.

07:58.644 --> 07:59.770
Where are you going, huh?

07:59.854 --> 08:00.897
[books clatter]

08:00.980 --> 08:03.024
- Oh jeez.
- [Won-jun] Ah!

08:03.107 --> 08:05.985
Ay! Oh! Oh!

08:06.068 --> 08:08.279
Ow! Ow! What the heck?

08:08.779 --> 08:11.324
- Oh! Ah! Ah!
- [stomping on floor]

08:12.992 --> 08:15.328
["Love Actually" by Daybreak
playing in Korean]

08:25.338 --> 08:26.714
[Won-jun] This goes here.

08:27.882 --> 08:28.758
There we go.

08:33.763 --> 08:34.972
[chuckles]

08:35.056 --> 08:36.265
This looks great.

08:42.438 --> 08:44.232
Organic pumpkin, huh?

08:58.412 --> 09:00.998
MINSONG NATIONAL UNIVERSITY
CIVIL ENGINEERING TOP SCHOLAR

09:01.082 --> 09:04.335
TUTOR

09:15.930 --> 09:16.806
[sighs]

09:26.357 --> 09:27.483
- [snips]
- [Won-jun] Ah!

09:31.320 --> 09:32.321
[sighs]

09:34.156 --> 09:35.116
[groans]

09:39.036 --> 09:40.871
KOREAN TUTOR
MINSONG KOR LIT FRESHMAN

09:41.706 --> 09:43.249
[girl] Look, there's still some left.

09:44.292 --> 09:45.418
[girl 2] Oh, that's great.

09:46.168 --> 09:47.587
- Here you go.
- [girl 2] Thank you.

09:48.337 --> 09:49.213
Hmm.

09:49.422 --> 09:51.132
Hey, do you see that boy's hoodie?

09:51.215 --> 09:54.010
He must be a superfan, huh?
Why would he wear that outside?

09:54.093 --> 09:56.262
- It's kind of cute, right?
- Obviously, cute.

09:56.345 --> 09:57.763
[line ringing]

10:05.813 --> 10:07.356
[gentle music playing]

10:08.441 --> 10:09.609
[ringing continues]

10:36.886 --> 10:37.720
[sighs]

10:39.889 --> 10:40.890
[keyboard clicking]

10:40.973 --> 10:43.684
THERE'S A STALKER ON THE SECOND FLOOR

11:17.093 --> 11:18.969
[phone vibrates]

11:19.679 --> 11:20.721
KOOK SU-JIN

11:21.681 --> 11:22.556
Kooksu, what is it?

11:22.640 --> 11:24.600
[Kooksu] Hey, bro!

11:24.684 --> 11:26.894
Get ready to bow and kiss my feet, bro!

11:26.977 --> 11:28.104
Kiss your feet?

11:29.271 --> 11:31.816
Someone's willing to pay
800,000 won for tutoring?

11:31.899 --> 11:33.317
Yeah, isn't that great?

11:33.401 --> 11:35.194
Every month and that's just for math.

11:35.277 --> 11:36.404
Isn't this freaking sweet?

11:36.487 --> 11:38.155
Uh, yeah. Can't believe it at all.

11:38.239 --> 11:41.075
That amount will cover
all of my rent and living expenses.

11:41.158 --> 11:43.244
CEO Kooksu, I don't know how to thank you.

11:43.327 --> 11:45.579
Can you please thank your mom for me
for the referral?

11:45.663 --> 11:47.665
How's your place, huh? Is it nice?

11:47.748 --> 11:51.419
♪ Screaming out so loud! ♪

11:51.502 --> 11:53.629
- ♪ It's so loud, so loud, baby… ♪
- What? Wait, what?

11:53.713 --> 11:55.005
♪ Screaming in my heart ♪

11:55.089 --> 11:57.007
♪ Ah, Dream Sweet, Lee Doona! ♪

11:57.091 --> 11:58.551
♪ You're my love forever, girl! ♪

11:58.634 --> 12:01.512
That's how much I love you, Doona!
I'm in love with you, okay? Yeah!

12:01.595 --> 12:03.639
- Jeez. What the hell?
- [Kooksu] Whoo!

12:03.723 --> 12:06.559
Didn't you say you threw their albums out
because you were done with them.

12:07.268 --> 12:10.354
It's not easy giving up
on something you love so much.

12:10.438 --> 12:11.689
Oh, Won-jun, hey.

12:11.772 --> 12:14.191
For your information,
I lent you that hoodie, remember?

12:14.275 --> 12:15.609
And I want it back, you hear?

12:15.693 --> 12:17.403
It was a limited-edition item.

12:17.486 --> 12:19.196
Doona won't have
new merch now for a while.

12:19.280 --> 12:20.698
Wait a second. What hoodie?

12:21.198 --> 12:23.117
You mean my birthday present for you?

12:25.077 --> 12:26.078
Uh, seriously?

12:26.162 --> 12:28.247
I was wearing this all day yesterday.

12:28.330 --> 12:30.583
What? You wore it out? Bro!

12:30.666 --> 12:33.836
READ
THERE'S A STALKER ON THE SECOND FLOOR

12:42.136 --> 12:43.137
- [sighs]
- [door beeps]

12:43.220 --> 12:45.848
[Won-jun] ♪ I'm gonna make
Some money, money ♪

12:46.807 --> 12:49.518
♪ Per subject, more money, money ♪

12:50.227 --> 12:53.355
♪ I'll sneak into your dreams ♪

12:53.439 --> 12:55.441
♪ I step, I… ♪

13:01.614 --> 13:02.782
What's your deal?

13:06.827 --> 13:08.329
[Won-jun thinking] Now I remember!

13:10.873 --> 13:12.917
You're Lee Doona! Dream Sweet!

13:13.000 --> 13:14.627
I just figured out who you were.

13:15.920 --> 13:18.214
- You really expect me to believe that?
- What?

13:18.297 --> 13:19.882
Sorry, but what did you mean by that?

13:23.594 --> 13:25.679
Would you stop the acting?
Seriously! You're a joke!

13:25.763 --> 13:26.889
Whoa!

13:29.183 --> 13:31.352
Oh! Are you insane?
That could've really hurt!

13:32.436 --> 13:34.104
Wow, you act like a child.

13:34.188 --> 13:35.356
What's that?

13:35.439 --> 13:38.150
- So how did you know I live here, huh?
- Well, I didn't.

13:39.026 --> 13:41.070
Where's your spy cam?
It's around here, right?

13:42.112 --> 13:43.614
What are you hoping to see?

13:44.990 --> 13:47.368
You're here 'cause you're stalking me,
isn't that right?

13:47.451 --> 13:49.745
Listen, I'm not a stalker. I swear.

13:49.829 --> 13:53.082
I have a friend who's a superfan.
That's why I recognize you. I promise.

13:54.458 --> 13:56.669
Look, I'm sorry. I'll stop talking.

14:02.591 --> 14:03.801
And just so you know,

14:04.593 --> 14:06.178
TWICE is my favorite band. TWICE.

14:06.262 --> 14:08.264
[curious music playing]

14:14.103 --> 14:15.646
[phone vibrates]

14:15.729 --> 14:17.273
MOM

14:17.356 --> 14:19.817
DECLINE - ACCEPT

14:22.027 --> 14:23.070
[sighs]

14:26.073 --> 14:29.577
In terms of math, I'm certain
you won't find a tutor that's better.

14:29.660 --> 14:32.663
And my expertise
is a result of my experience as a tutor.

14:32.746 --> 14:34.290
I'm truly confident.

14:34.373 --> 14:35.833
[teacup gently clatters]

14:36.417 --> 14:38.627
I think you're quite earnest, hmm?
I appreciate that.

14:40.087 --> 14:43.090
Then, um, can I start
the tutoring lessons next week?

14:43.966 --> 14:44.925
Mm-hmm.

14:45.593 --> 14:46.719
[chuckles]

14:46.802 --> 14:47.761
[door opens]

14:47.845 --> 14:49.263
- [woman] Oh, Mr. Lee!
- Yes?

14:50.264 --> 14:53.517
[sighs] You, uh… you forgot this.

14:53.601 --> 14:55.561
Oh. Thank you very much.

14:58.731 --> 15:00.357
[Won-jun whistling]

15:00.441 --> 15:02.109
[bicycle bell jingles]

15:05.571 --> 15:08.657
MINSONG NATIONAL UNIVERSITY
PREVIEW

15:11.452 --> 15:13.203
MATH TUTOR

15:14.371 --> 15:15.915
Excuse me. Are you looking for a…

15:18.626 --> 15:20.002
Oh, Won-jun, hey.

15:26.675 --> 15:29.136
It's been a while, hasn't it, Jin-ju?

15:31.889 --> 15:35.225
[pop music plays]

15:37.353 --> 15:38.520
Ah. Mmm.

15:38.604 --> 15:41.106
I almost didn't recognize you
because your hair is much shorter.

15:41.190 --> 15:44.026
Oh, really?
It's been like this for over a year.

15:47.029 --> 15:48.948
- Exactly.
- Ah.

15:49.031 --> 15:51.659
Um, uh, I know
we haven't seen each other for a while.

15:54.870 --> 15:57.414
Uh, for the record,
short hair suits you well.

15:58.040 --> 16:01.126
[chuckles] So where are you staying?
Are you still commuting here?

16:01.210 --> 16:04.213
I was until last year.
Now I share a co-ed house nearby.

16:04.296 --> 16:05.589
Ah.

16:07.049 --> 16:09.510
Oh, that's too bad.
I thought we could ride here together.

16:10.427 --> 16:12.012
Round trip, it's five hours.

16:12.096 --> 16:13.931
I'll probably go crazy commuting alone.

16:14.515 --> 16:15.391
What do you mean?

16:15.891 --> 16:17.601
I got into Minsong too.

16:20.020 --> 16:21.313
Hey! [chuckles]

16:21.397 --> 16:23.273
I finally got in. Where's the congrats?

16:23.357 --> 16:24.900
Oh, right. Uh…

16:25.609 --> 16:27.486
Cheers! [chuckles]

16:27.569 --> 16:29.488
[heartfelt music playing]

16:30.406 --> 16:32.199
[sighs] It's snowing.

16:34.910 --> 16:35.911
[chuckles]

16:40.958 --> 16:42.751
- It's so chilly.
- Uh…

16:42.835 --> 16:44.545
- [Jin-ju] Mmm.
- [bag unzips]

16:46.588 --> 16:48.841
- [Won-jun] Here.
- Oh, uh, are you sure?

16:48.924 --> 16:51.135
Take it. It's cold. And it's snowing too.

16:52.636 --> 16:54.138
All right. Thank you.

16:58.434 --> 17:00.686
- Nice to know you're still a sweet guy.
- [chuckles]

17:05.357 --> 17:06.775
Mmm, that's mine.

17:10.529 --> 17:11.780
And that's mine.

17:11.864 --> 17:12.948
KOREAN TUTOR FOR CSAT

17:13.032 --> 17:14.575
Oh, so you're the competition then.

17:14.658 --> 17:16.410
We've always been competitors, haven't we?

17:16.493 --> 17:18.162
Even though I've never won yet.

17:18.746 --> 17:20.247
[Jin-ju chuckles]

17:23.584 --> 17:24.543
Hmm.

17:27.588 --> 17:29.381
Anyway, how about we
get together more often

17:29.465 --> 17:30.758
since we're at the same school?

17:30.841 --> 17:31.925
Mmm, I'd like that.

17:32.009 --> 17:33.343
- [vehicle approaching]
- Hmm.

17:34.928 --> 17:36.180
Oh, that's my bus.

17:38.015 --> 17:39.767
- I'll see you later.
- [brakes squeak]

17:45.522 --> 17:46.857
[machine beeps]

17:46.940 --> 17:48.192
[door closes]

18:03.415 --> 18:04.333
Hmm.

18:07.795 --> 18:10.172
KOREAN TUTOR FOR CSAT
MINSONG KOR LIT FRESHMAN

18:10.255 --> 18:12.257
[emotional music playing]

18:26.563 --> 18:27.564
[sighs]

18:55.884 --> 18:57.678
Is she okay in this cold?

19:13.986 --> 19:14.945
[Doona whimpers]

19:25.330 --> 19:26.832
- Hey!
- Uh, yes?

19:35.465 --> 19:37.176
Don't ever sing my song again.

19:38.218 --> 19:39.845
Just so you know,
you're a horrible singer.

19:42.556 --> 19:45.392
If you so much as hum a lyric
of my song ever again, I'll…

19:45.475 --> 19:47.603
I'm gonna have to smash your head in.
You got it?

19:47.686 --> 19:48.979
Hmm, smash my head?

19:54.860 --> 19:56.028
[Doona sighs]

19:56.862 --> 19:57.946
[Won-jun] Whoa! Oh!

19:58.572 --> 19:59.698
Uh, hey.

19:59.781 --> 20:01.366
Can you hear me? Are you okay?

20:01.450 --> 20:03.452
[suspenseful music playing]

20:09.374 --> 20:12.294
[Won-jun] Uh, hi.
I'm at 21 Minsongdae Road.

20:12.377 --> 20:14.087
Someone passed out here.
She's unconscious.

20:15.005 --> 20:16.590
Please get here as soon as you can.

20:16.673 --> 20:18.717
Please hurry. Get here quickly.

20:19.218 --> 20:20.510
Yes, thank you. Yes.

20:25.849 --> 20:27.851
[siren blaring in distance]

20:29.019 --> 20:31.021
[people passing in hall]

20:42.282 --> 20:44.284
[indistinct background chatter]

20:48.247 --> 20:49.581
JOB HUNTING STUDY GROUP

20:49.665 --> 20:52.542
[Won-jun thinking]
Is this applicable only to seniors?

20:54.211 --> 20:55.462
- [Doona] Hey.
- Oh!

20:55.545 --> 20:57.714
Oh! You're awake.

20:57.798 --> 20:59.216
You're at the hospital right now.

21:00.926 --> 21:03.804
Oh, the, uh… the nurse
asked for you emergency contact earlier.

21:06.056 --> 21:07.182
I've got nobody.

21:10.018 --> 21:10.936
Well,

21:12.479 --> 21:14.398
you really should call your family, then.

21:15.399 --> 21:16.650
There's nobody, dude.

21:17.442 --> 21:19.695
Uh, how about your… manager, or--

21:19.778 --> 21:21.196
There's fucking nobody, okay?

21:27.661 --> 21:29.538
How come you're swearing?
People are around.

21:29.621 --> 21:30.914
Yeah, what's your point?

21:31.415 --> 21:33.583
- You don't swear at all?
- No, I don't at all.

21:34.418 --> 21:36.545
I'm also not a celebrity, unlike someone.

21:37.421 --> 21:38.755
Yeah, well, I'm not now either.

21:46.388 --> 21:49.016
Miss Lee Doona, is your next of kin here?

21:50.809 --> 21:52.060
Miss Lee Doona.

21:52.769 --> 21:55.022
Uh, so… so I'm her sibling, actually.

21:55.105 --> 21:56.857
You can speak to me about everything.

21:56.940 --> 21:58.525
Could you please come with me, then?

22:04.406 --> 22:08.201
Thanks to your quick action,
there are no complications at this time.

22:08.285 --> 22:10.996
However, her body temperature
is a bit on the low side,

22:11.079 --> 22:14.624
so please make sure her head,
hands, and feet always stay warm.

22:14.708 --> 22:17.419
Have her use a dry blanket,
and most importantly,

22:17.502 --> 22:19.796
make sure she always
has socks on her feet.

22:19.880 --> 22:23.175
Having her drink warm beverages
will also help the recovery process.

22:23.258 --> 22:24.301
[Won-jun] Okay, got it.

22:24.384 --> 22:27.929
Oh, also, could she be having
any internal problems at all?

22:28.430 --> 22:30.599
Do you know
if she'll need other prognostic testing?

22:30.682 --> 22:33.685
[nurse] No, no further tests
are required at this time.

22:33.769 --> 22:37.356
Oh, sorry, do you have
a phone charger I maybe could borrow?

22:37.439 --> 22:39.941
- [nurse] Uh, just a moment.
- [Won-jun] Thank you.

22:50.911 --> 22:52.120
They said you needed socks.

22:54.790 --> 22:57.209
- I'd prefer if you put them on for me.
- I should?

22:58.251 --> 22:59.503
You're my sibling.

23:02.255 --> 23:03.256
Um, right.

23:07.594 --> 23:09.596
- [unwrapping socks]
- [beeping in hall]

23:11.056 --> 23:12.265
Okay, just bear with me.

23:27.531 --> 23:30.158
It'll be just a little longer. Sorry.

23:33.870 --> 23:35.288
Huh?

23:35.372 --> 23:37.707
[curious music playing]

23:39.334 --> 23:41.294
[Doona] They didn't have
any normal sleeping socks?

23:41.378 --> 23:42.254
What's that?

23:42.337 --> 23:44.965
You couldn't find proper bed socks
that were more plain?

23:45.549 --> 23:47.676
- I prefer my belongings to look ordinary.
- [chuckles]

23:49.428 --> 23:50.554
What's funny?

23:51.179 --> 23:52.556
Um, oh, nothing.

23:54.224 --> 23:56.518
You claim you prefer ordinary things,
but it's strange

23:56.601 --> 23:58.645
because you're not
an ordinary girl at all.

23:59.980 --> 24:03.775
Did you know… sleeping socks sometimes
make you sweat more during the night?

24:04.359 --> 24:05.777
That can make you feel colder.

24:05.861 --> 24:07.446
So these will be better for you.

24:07.529 --> 24:09.573
Anyway, the other socks were
old-men socks,

24:09.656 --> 24:10.949
so pink was the best option.

24:21.376 --> 24:23.962
So, by the way, what's your name,
my fake sibling?

24:24.045 --> 24:25.046
Who, me?

24:30.135 --> 24:32.762
Uh, that's personal information.

24:42.898 --> 24:44.900
[phone ringing]

24:50.197 --> 24:52.616
KOOK SU-JIN

24:54.618 --> 24:55.869
Hey, Kooksu.

24:55.952 --> 24:58.205
Hey, when did you begin smoking?

24:58.288 --> 24:59.206
Huh?

24:59.915 --> 25:01.124
I don't smoke, okay?

25:01.625 --> 25:02.667
Why do you ask?

25:02.751 --> 25:06.379
My mom's friend said to tell you
to forget about the tutoring gig.

25:08.340 --> 25:09.758
- What?
- [Kooksu] You jackass!

25:09.841 --> 25:12.302
She asked me to confirm
that you're not a smoker three times,

25:12.385 --> 25:13.845
I told her you don't over and over.

25:13.929 --> 25:16.097
But then, she told me
she had picked up your scarf,

25:16.181 --> 25:17.599
and it reeked of cigarettes.

25:22.854 --> 25:24.064
[groans]

25:29.194 --> 25:30.111
[sighs]

25:30.779 --> 25:32.155
I can't believe this happened.

25:32.864 --> 25:34.449
All that money just gone.

25:38.036 --> 25:39.204
[phone chimes]

25:44.167 --> 25:46.753
YOUR ITEM HAS BEEN DELIVERED

25:46.836 --> 25:47.712
[door beeps]

25:52.008 --> 25:53.134
[door beeps]

25:58.473 --> 25:59.891
[Doona] Hi, Won-jun.

25:59.975 --> 26:01.977
[curious music playing]

26:03.853 --> 26:05.522
Did you have breakfast yet?

26:05.605 --> 26:07.524
If not,
why don't we share a meal together?

26:07.607 --> 26:11.319
Wait, uh…
Hey, is that my package by any chance?

26:13.989 --> 26:14.990
Oh.

26:20.036 --> 26:20.954
What did you buy, huh?

26:21.037 --> 26:23.164
It's something super cushy, right?

26:23.248 --> 26:25.542
No, but why would you sit
on someone else's package?

26:25.625 --> 26:28.545
Oh, I'm starving right now.
So what should we get?

26:28.628 --> 26:30.005
I'm going inside now.

26:37.220 --> 26:38.054
Hmm?

26:41.182 --> 26:43.768
[Won-jun] And that was the day
she started waiting for me.

26:44.352 --> 26:45.270
[door beeps]

26:47.480 --> 26:48.315
[door beeps]

26:50.317 --> 26:53.153
- [Won-jun] Oh!
- Hi, Won-jun. Have you had breakfast yet?

26:53.236 --> 26:55.238
There's a tteokbokki place.
Let's go, yeah?

26:55.322 --> 26:56.239
[clears throat]

26:56.906 --> 26:57.824
Hey, Won-jun!

27:01.161 --> 27:03.622
Let's share a combo meal. [laughs]

27:03.705 --> 27:05.999
- [door beeps]
- Won-jun! Come on! Let's eat!

27:06.833 --> 27:08.835
[alarm clocking chiming]

27:16.259 --> 27:17.093
[grunts]

27:19.721 --> 27:21.348
She's driving me crazy.

27:26.561 --> 27:28.021
Oh, crap, she's here.

27:28.104 --> 27:29.439
[Doona] Good evening.

27:32.233 --> 27:33.234
Uh, good evening.

27:33.318 --> 27:36.613
If you're here to do some laundry,
go ahead. Don't mind me.

27:51.586 --> 27:52.462
[sniffs]

28:02.013 --> 28:03.014
Uh…

28:12.399 --> 28:14.984
Oh! Uh, oh, this?

28:15.068 --> 28:17.237
I had bought this for my friend
as his birthday present.

28:17.320 --> 28:19.155
He let me borrow it,
but I need to return it.

28:19.239 --> 28:21.783
And I only had it on that day
because it was super cold

28:21.866 --> 28:23.410
and the fleece lining kept me warm.

28:23.493 --> 28:24.369
Was I speaking?

28:24.452 --> 28:26.746
- I don't want you to get the wrong idea.
- [Doona] I won't.

28:26.830 --> 28:29.958
You said you're not a fan.
So you're not a fan.

28:39.092 --> 28:41.553
You dress well
for a civil engineering major, you know?

28:42.470 --> 28:44.681
Does your girlfriend
help you choose your outfits?

28:44.764 --> 28:46.307
No, I don't have one yet.

28:49.310 --> 28:51.896
I'm hungry. Should we grab something?

28:54.733 --> 28:57.527
Um… well, there's something
I wanna ask first.

28:58.278 --> 29:01.156
Mmm… so are you, um,

29:01.656 --> 29:02.782
maybe falling for me?

29:02.866 --> 29:04.826
Because it's starting
to feel like you are.

29:08.037 --> 29:09.956
If so, please don't fall for me.

29:10.039 --> 29:12.083
Really,
it's making me uncomfortable, okay?

29:14.210 --> 29:15.170
[laughing]

29:23.052 --> 29:24.637
What's so funny? Why are you laughing?

29:26.306 --> 29:28.183
Won-jun, you're hilarious.

29:28.767 --> 29:30.769
[whimsical music playing]

29:31.394 --> 29:33.897
Ah, it's been a long time
since I've laughed.

29:33.980 --> 29:35.982
[laughs]

29:36.900 --> 29:38.401
- Hey.
- Yes?

29:38.485 --> 29:42.363
I won't end up falling for you.
It's never happening, okay? [laughs]

29:42.447 --> 29:44.407
Well, that was unnecessary to say.

29:46.409 --> 29:49.537
Let's just hang out.
I wanna be your friend, okay?

29:50.163 --> 29:52.540
Oh, you do? But why?

29:52.624 --> 29:54.125
Because I don't have any here.

29:56.336 --> 29:57.587
Well, uh…

29:57.670 --> 29:59.881
Oh, um, well,
the whole downstairs is all girls.

29:59.964 --> 30:01.591
You can ask one of them to be your friend.

30:01.674 --> 30:04.344
Downstairs? The entire floor is all mine.

30:05.512 --> 30:08.973
Wow, you're pretty loaded.
Now I very much wanna be your best friend.

30:09.057 --> 30:10.809
You mean it?
I can call you whenever I want?

30:10.892 --> 30:12.018
Uh, you can't, no.

30:12.101 --> 30:13.520
You're a tough nut to crack.

30:13.603 --> 30:14.729
Yes, I suppose that's true.

30:17.148 --> 30:18.942
I guess there's no hope then.

30:19.025 --> 30:22.153
If a superfan or stalker attacks me
and I die, it'll be all your fault, hmm?

30:23.071 --> 30:25.740
- Wait, but how would it be my fault?
- [Doona] The sun's coming up.

30:25.824 --> 30:27.617
I have to make a wish now.
Stop bothering me.

30:27.700 --> 30:29.369
Now hold on.
Who was bothering who first?

30:31.663 --> 30:32.580
[sighs]

30:40.588 --> 30:42.340
[birds chirping]

30:55.937 --> 30:57.939
[emotional music playing]

31:10.034 --> 31:11.160
[Doona sighs]

31:15.415 --> 31:16.291
[sighs]

31:18.668 --> 31:19.669
[grunts softly]

31:28.678 --> 31:29.971
[thinking] I can't.

31:31.014 --> 31:32.557
- [Doona] Hey.
- Huh?

31:33.725 --> 31:34.851
You forgot your underwear.

31:35.602 --> 31:36.769
Huh? Uh…

31:39.022 --> 31:40.064
[Doona chuckles]

31:46.487 --> 31:47.405
[groans]

31:48.489 --> 31:50.074
I really wish I could move out.

32:02.462 --> 32:03.296
Hmm?

32:12.847 --> 32:14.140
[girl] Kim Jin-ju!

32:14.223 --> 32:15.099
Jin-ju!

32:15.183 --> 32:17.518
- [girl 2] Hey, Jin-ju!
- [girl] Sorry we're late.

32:17.602 --> 32:19.062
- Let's eat.
- [girl 2] Is it good?

32:20.813 --> 32:22.482
[girl] Uh, what does "meh" mean?

32:26.736 --> 32:27.862
[Jin-ju] Lee Won-jun.

32:30.698 --> 32:32.241
- Hey.
- Oh.

32:32.825 --> 32:35.536
[chuckles] You didn't hear?
I was calling you.

32:36.120 --> 32:38.498
- I forgot to give back your scarf.
- You can hold onto that.

32:38.581 --> 32:40.500
No, it's okay. It smells like cigarettes.

32:41.417 --> 32:42.502
- Ah.
- [Jin-ju] Oh.

32:45.004 --> 32:46.756
Hey, let me take a look for you.

32:58.101 --> 32:59.477
Mmm, you got it.

33:01.229 --> 33:02.063
[Jin-ju chuckles]

33:02.814 --> 33:03.648
See you later.

33:04.273 --> 33:05.108
Mm-hmm.

33:06.567 --> 33:08.361
- [girl] Who was that? Who was that?
- What? Who?

33:08.444 --> 33:10.863
- Who is he?
- Oh, stop. Just someone I know.

33:10.947 --> 33:12.448
[girl] Too cute to just be someone.

33:12.532 --> 33:14.617
It looked like you guys
definitely had chemistry.

33:14.701 --> 33:16.577
[Won-jun thinking] "Just someone I know."

33:20.289 --> 33:22.333
[Won-jun]
Can't you just tell her I don't smoke?

33:22.417 --> 33:24.711
This friend I have…
Ah! No! What am I saying?

33:24.794 --> 33:26.337
This strange girl at my place…

33:27.005 --> 33:28.840
Ah, man, I don't smoke, okay?

33:30.675 --> 33:31.509
Already?

33:32.552 --> 33:33.845
She found a tutor?

33:33.928 --> 33:35.888
[woman] Ten total.
That'll be 70,000 won, please.

33:36.973 --> 33:39.058
- There you go. Thank you.
- [woman] Yes, thanks.

33:39.142 --> 33:41.144
[calm upbeat music playing]

34:04.542 --> 34:07.336
PART-TIMERS WANTED
RECRUITING STAFF MEMBERS FOR CAFÉ 1890

34:09.172 --> 34:10.048
Hello, sir.

34:13.676 --> 34:15.386
- [man] Take it down.
- What?

34:16.179 --> 34:17.221
You better take it down.

34:17.305 --> 34:19.432
Oh, can I not hang these flyers here?

34:19.515 --> 34:22.894
Don't you know you need a little stamp
like this, and it's not free.

34:22.977 --> 34:25.104
You think you can post stuff
without permission, huh?

34:49.337 --> 34:51.422
[Kooksu] Tutoring? That's a piece of cake.

34:51.506 --> 34:56.135
Ladies and gentlemen,
Yangjin's top brain! Our greatest tutor!

34:56.219 --> 34:58.471
Lee Won-jun!

34:58.554 --> 34:59.472
Whoo!

35:00.598 --> 35:02.475
[exhales] So I'll come visit, okay?

35:02.558 --> 35:05.603
What for? Don't forget to take
the organic pumpkin juice with you.

35:05.686 --> 35:07.313
It's in the refrigerator, okay?

35:08.940 --> 35:10.149
Hey, Won-jun!

35:10.233 --> 35:11.109
Huh?

35:11.651 --> 35:13.569
If you get a girlfriend, send pics, okay?

35:13.653 --> 35:15.446
[Won-jun] Get back inside! It's freezing!

35:15.530 --> 35:17.740
And make sure
you take your medicine on time!

35:17.824 --> 35:19.826
[emotional music playing]

35:34.882 --> 35:35.716
Oh!

35:36.217 --> 35:40.096
MATH TUTOR

35:40.179 --> 35:41.556
[phone vibrating]

35:41.639 --> 35:42.473
Hmm?

35:46.561 --> 35:47.603
Um, yes, hello?

35:48.604 --> 35:49.730
Hello? Are you there?

35:51.315 --> 35:53.860
[woman] Hello.
I got your phone number from your flier.

35:54.610 --> 35:56.028
Yes. Yes. How can I help you?

35:56.112 --> 35:58.072
[woman] By any chance, I was wondering

35:58.156 --> 35:59.740
if you would be able to

36:01.117 --> 36:03.744
go out for a meal with me sometime?

36:03.828 --> 36:04.996
[knocking on glass]

36:05.788 --> 36:07.915
[chuckles] Hey!

36:07.999 --> 36:10.001
MATH TUTOR

36:10.084 --> 36:11.919
[laughing]

36:17.508 --> 36:18.467
[sighs]

36:22.013 --> 36:22.930
Are you still mad?

36:23.890 --> 36:24.724
Not at all.

36:24.807 --> 36:26.517
You're still mad. I can totally tell.

36:26.601 --> 36:29.770
Hey, you can be mad at me.
I wanna see what you're like.

36:30.521 --> 36:32.106
Although, I don't know why you're angry.

36:32.190 --> 36:34.650
Didn't you put the fliers up
so people would give you a call?

36:36.152 --> 36:36.986
Doona, listen.

36:38.154 --> 36:41.949
Are you, like, crazy bored or what?
Is this some kind of joke or something?

36:43.117 --> 36:46.120
You can do almost anything you want to
because you have all the money and time

36:46.204 --> 36:47.580
and don't need to work like I do.

36:47.663 --> 36:49.749
You don't have to care
about how you live your life.

36:49.832 --> 36:50.958
Congratulations.

36:51.792 --> 36:54.837
Guess what, though. Not everyone
has the same luxury as you do.

36:54.921 --> 36:57.298
I desperately need a job
and need to study hard for my career.

36:57.381 --> 36:58.424
Don't you get it?

36:58.507 --> 37:00.968
I have so much on my plate at the moment.

37:01.052 --> 37:02.720
So if you have any ounce of decency,

37:02.803 --> 37:05.890
can you just leave me alone and stop
following me around like a lost girl.

37:07.058 --> 37:10.436
I don't find any of this
the slightest bit amusing.

37:13.856 --> 37:15.399
That was disappointing. Seriously.

37:16.108 --> 37:17.318
I expected more, Won-jun.

37:17.902 --> 37:19.612
You're pretty terrible at…

37:20.112 --> 37:21.197
at getting mad, hmm?

37:21.697 --> 37:23.950
But I understand everything.

37:29.789 --> 37:31.332
- [keypad beeping]
- [door beeps]

37:31.415 --> 37:32.458
[door opens]

37:33.751 --> 37:35.586
- [door closes]
- [panting]

37:44.553 --> 37:45.471
[door beeps]

37:57.525 --> 37:58.442
[scoffs]

38:06.075 --> 38:06.993
[sighs]

38:22.967 --> 38:24.969
[indistinct chatter on TV]

38:41.444 --> 38:42.486
- [door squeaks]
- Oh.

38:44.822 --> 38:46.824
[door squeaking]

38:49.618 --> 38:50.536
Uh, hello?

38:56.917 --> 38:58.377
Miss Doona, are you here?

38:59.420 --> 39:03.466
Um… how about we get a meal
sometime in the near future?

39:03.549 --> 39:05.301
Like, um, whenever you feel like it.

39:06.093 --> 39:07.053
And I'll treat you.

39:09.096 --> 39:10.681
Well, when I get a tutoring gig.

39:16.020 --> 39:18.647
- Oh jeez. My goodness.
- [crunching]

39:23.444 --> 39:24.528
[grunts]

39:33.662 --> 39:36.540
